{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/7941","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:57:14.199384+00:00","comments":[],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Describe the bug\n\nWhen converting layouts via the swizzling path, boolean (i1) values are recovered by truncating from i8 to i1. This truncation keeps only the least significant bit (LSB), so a byte like 0x02 becomes false.\nThe code with bug below:\n```C++\nSmallVector<Value> transferWithinBlockSwizzlingImpl(\n    Location loc, ConversionPatternRewriter &rewriter,\n    const LinearLayout &srcLayout, const LinearLayout &dstLayout,\n    ArrayRef<Value> inVals, Type llvmElemTy, Value smemBase) const {\n  ...\n  if (llvmElemTy.getIntOrFloatBitWidth() < 8) {\n    // Upcast to i8\n    auto i8ElemTy = i8_ty;\n    auto newInVals = llvm::to_vector(llvm::map_range(\n        inVals, [&](Value v) { return b.zext(i8ElemTy, v).getResult(); }));\n    auto outVals = transferWithinBlockSwizzlingImpl(\n        loc, rewriter, srcLayout, dstLayout, newInVals, i8ElemTy, smemBase);\n    for (auto &v : outVals) {\n      v = b.trunc(llvmElemTy, v);  // Truncates to LSB only (drops higher-order bits)\n    }\n    return outVals;\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\nThis leads to incorrect boolean handling: any non-zero byte with the LSB unset (e.g., 0x02) is read as false.\n\n### Environment details\n\nTriton: 3.4\nGPU: (XPU device)","closed_at":"2025-12-08T12:44:24Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99736820?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdziurdz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdziurdz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdziurdz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdziurdz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wdziurdz","id":99736820,"login":"wdziurdz","node_id":"U_kgDOBfHc9A","organizations_url":"https: