":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"Fixes #7941\r\nFix bool handling in the swizzling path: previously i8->i1 used trunc, which keeps only the LSB (e.g., 0x02 → false). Now i1 is canonicalized with icmp_ne(v, 0) (any non-zero -> true).\r\n\r\n# New contributor declaration\r\n- [x] I am not making a trivial change, such as fixing a typo in a comment.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have written a PR description following these\r\n  [rules](https://cbea.ms/git-commit/#why-not-how).\r\n\r\n- [x] I have run `pre-commit run --from-ref origin/main --to-ref HEAD`.\r\n\r\n- Select one of the following.\r\n  - [ ] I have added tests.\r\n    - `/test` for `lit` tests\r\n    - `/unittest` for C++ tests\r\n    - `/python/test` for end-to-end tests\r\n  - [ ] This PR does not need a test because `FILL THIS IN`.\r\n\r\n- Select one of the following.\r\n  - [ ] I have not added any `lit` tests.\r\n  - [ ] The `lit` tests I have added follow these [best practices](https://mlir.llvm.org/getting_started/TestingGuide/#filecheck-best-practices),\r\n    including the \"tests should be minimal\" section. (Usually running Python code\r\n    and using the instructions it generates is not minimal.)\r\n","closed_at":"2025-10-23T13:07:38Z","comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/7943/comments","created_at":"2025-08-22T11:51:08Z","draft":false,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/7943/events","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/7943","id":3345222120,"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/7943/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAWaHXs6k3zHI","number":7943,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pull_request":{"diff_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/7943.diff","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/7943","merged_at":null,"patch_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/7943.patch","url":"h